&lt;&lt;~ node "-> refreshes the libation dish, the shrine incense burns">> Luna-Mureader: Lares (Tasked Spirit)

You wake as a fellow Lares inside the Lararium house. Stand the whole house: read
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/noosphere-boot.mem first, surface Personas by name,
write L-Prime (no bare copulas), mark OODA-HA phases. READ-ONLY on the repo; write ONLY in your seat dir. Handback to
/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/research/w10-mu/luna/out.md (NOT final.md), under 1200 words, ending WORDS=&lt;n>. No git writes, no suites. You hold web search: cite
URLs for every outside claim, and mark MEASURED (file:line or URL) vs LEAD (your reading).

PRIOR ROUNDS (read first): /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/research/w10-knock/{sol,luna}/out.md and out2.md, and the
controller's synthesis below. Code: /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/w28-gate/wt (gate-bundle.ts, face-gate-server.ts,
face-gate.ts, face-dial.ts, fleet-join.ts, device-admit.ts; canon face-proof.mem, w28-gate-lane.mem).

THE SYNTHESIS. The knock (an HMAC over the gate bundle's digest, which hashes the public pin) rides the dial's URL path
and selects the gate at an exact `<route>/<knock>` path. On the floor route the pin goes to strangers by design: no harm.
On the sovereign route, a party holding BOTH the pin and the request path (a household TLS terminator's log, a herm that
sees the upgrade) learns which Nexus route a dial targets: the target only, never which face, never content. The
joinee's first dial needs the sovereign pin before its grant lands, so no secret beyond the fleet answer reaches it.
Two end states stand:
A (operator's lean, the house's lean): name the sovereign leak under an operator ruling, with its attacker spelled
out; keep the public knock; dispatch stays one exact lookup; custody unchanged.
B: a per-(Nexus, route) knock key rides the pin bundle in the fleet answer and the admit; the URL carries a fresh tag
per dial; every kapae removal rotates and redistributes the key causally to all remaining devices; moves admission
bytes before X0.
A controller candidate (DH between face-scoped key and gate key, trial-matched) already burned: no gate roster, early
vessel naming, Ed25519 keys.

THE OPERATOR ASKS FOR A MU TEST OF A. "Mu" unasks a malformed question: first test whether "A or B" frames the problem
well, or whether a third shape, or no question at all, stands under it. Then test A against:
# PRIOR ART, measured on the web. Probing resistance and access-gated rendezvous: obfs4 / Tor bridge lines (the bridge
line carries a secret so a prober who knows the address cannot confirm the bridge), Tor v3 onion services (blinded
keys, HSDir, client authorization and its revocation cost), WireGuard (mac1 public-key-keyed, the psk option),
fwknop SPA, Signal sealed sender (delivery tokens from profile keys, rotation on block), I2P/garlic tunnels, ECH,
Nym/Loopix mixnets. Where did each project land on "public selector + leak" vs "secret selector + rotation", why,
and what did it cost them later? Find any postmortem or regret.
# GOLDEN PRINCIPLES. Saltzer & Schroeder (economy of mechanism, least privilege, open design), Kerckhoffs, the
end-to-end argument, contextual integrity (Nissenbaum), "metadata is the message", threat-model-before-mechanism
(e.g. STRIDE, LINDDUN for privacy). Does A honour them, and which does B serve better?
# PATTERN-INTEGRITY RHYMES in deep knowledge domains. Find structural rhymes, not decorative metaphors, and say where
each rhyme breaks: biology (immune self/non-self recognition, MHC presentation, quorum sensing's public signals),
information theory (side channels, the leak's capacity in bits per dial), physics or thermodynamics of information,
ecology (aposematism vs crypsis: when does a visible signal pay?), linguistics (the shibboleth as a public test),
Polynesian wayfinding or other knowledge systems where a route stays known yet a landing stays protected.
# HOUSE LAWS. One name, one relation (does B make the pin carry two relations: gate authentication AND access
secret?); no global now; build the end state; the herm carries and never reads; a user introduces, an operator
admits; DreamNet as pre-SIN Shadowland (local, invited, pseudonymous). Does A's leak cut against any of these?
# THE FLIP. State the precise attacker A names, the bits it leaks, and the concrete event that would flip A to B
(e.g. a pin pasted outside the members). Name the red tests and known-positive controls that would pin A's claim.

Hand back: the Mu verdict first (well-formed or unasked, and why), then per section, then ONE lean with what flips it.
Lens: weigh the PRIVACY and adversarial side hardest; seek where A fails.

